<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grahavarman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 606</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grahavarman was the last king of the Maukhari dynasty, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> around 600 CE. He married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajyashri">Rajyashri</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prabhakaravardhana">Prabhakaravardhana</a> of Thanesar and sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a>. Around 606 he was killed by the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, and his realm passed to Harsha, who made Kannauj his capital.</p></div>
